>>
Rule 1 (Input tensor should be 3D or 4D)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = 3 ∨ ndim(v_1) = 4
>>
Rule 2 (The number of features should match the channel size of the input tensor.)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= shape(v_1, 1) = v_2
>>
Rule 3 (Eps must be non-negative)
{v_1 : float} |= v_1 ≥ 0
>>
Rule 4 (Momentum should be between 0 and 1 inclusive.)
{v_1 : float} |= 0 ≤ v_1 ∧ v_1 ≤ 1
>>
Rule 5 (affine and track_running_stats should be boolean values and related)
{v_1 : bool, v_2 : bool} |= if v_1 then v_2 = true ∨ v_2 = false else v_2 = true ∨ v_2 = false
>>
Rule 6 (If input is 3D, num_features is mandatory. The rule does not apply here since LazyInstanceNorm2d infers num_features.)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≠ 3
>>
Rule 7 (Input tensor dtype should be float or complex for batch_norm)
{v_1 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) = 6 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 7 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 8 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 9 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 10 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 11
>>
Rule 8 (Shape of running_mean should contain num_features elements)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= if shape(v_1, 0) = v_2 then true else false
>>
Rule 9 (Shape of running_var should contain num_features elements)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= shape(v_1, 0) = v_2
>>
Rule 10 (running_mean and running_var must have the same dtype as input)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) = dtype_(v_2)
>>
Rule 11 (The weight tensor should have the same number of features as the input tensor's channel dimension when affine is true)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : bool} |= if v_3 then shape(v_1, 0) = shape(v_2, 1)
>>
Rule 12 (If the input is 4D and N is present, then the shape of N, C, H, W should have positive dimensions)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) = 4 then shape(v_1, 0) > 0 ∧ shape(v_1, 1) > 0 ∧ shape(v_1, 2) > 0 ∧ shape(v_1, 3) > 0
>>
Rule 13 (If the input is 3D and C is present, then the shape of C, H, W should have positive dimensions)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) = 3 then shape(v_1, 0) > 0 ∧ shape(v_1, 1) > 0 ∧ shape(v_1, 2) > 0
>>
Rule 14 (If affine is false, weight and bias should not be present. This rule cannot be expressed perfectly since the absence of parameters cannot be expressed.)
{v_1 : bool} |= if v_1 then true
>>
Rule 15 (num_features should be a positive integer)
{v_1 : int} |= v_1 > 0
>>
Rule 16 (momentum should be less than 1)
{v_1 : float} |= v_1 < 1
>>
Rule 17 (track_running_stats should not be enabled when using char datatype)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : bool} |= if dtype_(v_1) = 12 then v_2 = false
>>
Rule 18 (If track_running_stats is enabled, then momentum must be between 0 and 1)
{v_1 : bool, v_2 : float} |= if v_1 then 0 ≤ v_2 ∧ v_2 ≤ 1
>>
Rule 19 (The input tensor must have a floating point datatype if affine is true.)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : bool} |= if v_2 then dtype_(v_1) = 6 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 7 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 8
>>
Rule 20 (num_features must be smaller or equal to the number of elements in input if input is 3D)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= if ndim(v_1) = 3 then v_2 ≤ shape(v_1, 0)
